  "team": "Georgia",
  "season": 2021,
  "coverage_notes": "SOURCES USED. (1) Wikipedia team-season page https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_Georgia_Bulldogs_football_team — infobox, \"Coaching staff\" table (which cites \"2021 Georgia Bulldogs Football Media Guide, p. 2\"), and the roster-footer staff list (~38 names). (2) Wayback snapshot of the official athletics site's 2021 football roster page, 2021-10-26 — https://web.archive.org/web/20211026231938/https://georgiadogs.com/sports/football/roster/2021 — which embeds the complete \"Football Coaching Staff\" (11) and \"Football Support Staff\" (45) directories. (3) Wayback snapshot of the athletics-wide staff directory, 2021-08-07 — https://web.archive.org/web/20210807071240/https://georgiadogs.com/staff-directory — whose \"Football\" and \"Strength and Conditioning - Football\" sections add 16 deeper names (graduate assistants, student assistants, video staff, sports-science analyst, performance chef, assistant equipment director, nutrition intern) that the roster-page directory omits. Total: 72 documented people.\n\nQUOTE MECHANICS. Quotes from the two georgiadogs.com Wayback pages are the name and title as they appear in adjacent DOM nodes; in the page's extracted text they are contiguous once runs of whitespace are collapsed to single spaces (verified programmatically — every quote below was string-matched against the whitespace-normalized text of its own URL). Wikipedia quotes are taken from the rendered roster-footer list lines and likewise verified. Note the georgiadogs pages render Bryant Gross-Armiento's surname with spaces (\"Bryant Gross - Armiento\"), and several titles use an en dash (–) rather than a hyphen; both are reproduced exactly.\n\nWHAT I COULD NOT DOCUMENT. (a) Medical/athletic-training staff. UGA's staff directory lists \"Athletic Training/Sports Medicine\" as an athletics-wide unit (Ron Courson, Anna Randa, and ~17 associate/assistant athletic trainers) with no sport assignment shown, so I could not source any individual as 2021 football medical staff. No football-specific medical rows are included rather than guess. (b) The 2021 Georgia football media guide itself — Wikipedia cites it, but I could not retrieve the guide PDF via archive.org (only fragmentary history PDFs were archived), so no rows rest on it. (c) A December 2021/January 2022 snapshot of the staff directory. The support-staff tiers are documented from August and October 2021 snapshots, so a small number of the deepest support roles (student assistants, video interns) could in principle have turned over before the January 10, 2022 title game; I found no documentation of any such departure. (d) Web search was unavailable this session (budget exhausted), so contemporary news articles could not be searched for hire/departure announcements beyond the Dan Lanning case, which is sourced from his Wikipedia article.\n\nNAME/ROLE DISCREPANCIES. Wikipedia spells the assistant strength coach \"Rodney Price\"; the official UGA site spells him \"Rodney Prince\" — I used the official spelling. Wikipedia lists Matt Godwin twice under two different titles (\"Player personnel coordinator\" and \"Director, player personnel\"); he is one person and appears once here. Rashawn Scott is titled \"Intern - Offense\" on the October roster page and \"Offensive Assistant\" in the August staff directory; both sources are attached. Will Muschamp was an analyst in 2021 (he was promoted to an on-field role only in 2022) and is categorized as analyst accordingly.\n\nCATEGORY JUDGMENT CALLS. Titles worded \"Defensive Assistant\" / \"Offensive Assistant\" / \"Special Teams Assistant\" (Murphy, Russell, Ray) are off-field analyst-tier roles at Georgia and are mapped to analyst, as is the \"Sports Science Data Analyst\". Creative/video/technology and recruiting/personnel/administration roles are mapped to ops. Nutrition staff and the performance chef are mapped to other rather than medical, since they sit in performance nutrition, not sports medicine. \"Student Assistant\" and intern titles are mapped to other; only explicit \"Graduate Assistant\"/\"GA\" titles are mapped to gradasst.",
